            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Arabic for to convict, then the Arabic for innocence."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ساحر",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ساحر — sāḥir — \"a magician, a sorcerer\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "حول الساحر الأمير إلى ضفدع. ḥawwala as-sāḥir al-amīr ilā ḍifdaʿ. The magician turned the prince into a frog."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Plural: سحرة, saḥara."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Of a place or a smile, ساحر (sāḥir) is enchanting."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ساحر (sāḥir) is built on the native Arabic root s-ḥ-r (Lane), \"to bewitch, to enchant\"; siḥr is magic and sāḥir the one who works it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
            }
          ]
        },
