          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "غول (ghūl) is built on the native Arabic root gh-w-l (Lane), \"to take and destroy without warning\". Lane gives ghūl as a being of the desert believed to lead travellers astray."
            }
          ]
